From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 22:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: reject ambiguous direct peer routes

A direct virtual port shared by MLO links can have references to several
PPE direct-switch nodes.  Falling back to its currently programmed static
queue when the destination peer is not mapped can silently send a flow to
the wrong radio.

Keep the fallback when exactly one node owns the virtual port, but reject
flow installation until peer routing is known when ownership is ambiguous.
The peer is normally registered before its first routed flow, so this only
turns an association race into a software-path fallback.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/tree/87bb9b326dfe7ddafb2cc8bc588e74d552a2a9b5
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.c
@@ -794,6 +794,7 @@ int ppe_vp_ds_node_get(struct ppe_device
 	struct ppe_vp *vp = ppe_dev->vp;
 	struct ppe_vp_peer *peer;
 	int i = port - PPE_VP_PORT_BASE;
+	int fallback = PPE_VP_DS_NODE_NONE;
 	int node;
 
 	if (!vp || i < 0 || i >= PPE_VP_SLOTS)
@@ -806,7 +807,24 @@ int ppe_vp_ds_node_get(struct ppe_device
 	}
 
 	peer = ppe_vp_ds_peer_find(vp, port, addr);
-	node = peer ? peer->node : vp->slots[i].ds_node;
+	if (peer) {
+		node = peer->node;
+	} else {
+		/* A single-node VP has an unambiguous static queue.  A shared
+		 * MLO VP needs a peer mapping because its static queue only
+		 * identifies one of several possible radios.
+		 */
+		for (node = 0; node < PPE_VP_DS_NODES; node++) {
+			if (!vp->slots[i].ds_node_refs[node])
+				continue;
+			if (fallback != PPE_VP_DS_NODE_NONE) {
+				node = -ENOENT;
+				goto out;
+			}
+			fallback = node;
+		}
+		node = fallback;
+	}
 	if (node < 0 || node >= PPE_VP_DS_NODES ||
 	    !vp->slots[i].ds_node_refs[node] || !vp->ds_node_up[node])
 		node = -ENETDOWN;
